---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Spoons from '../components/Spoons.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import NewsletterCTA from '../components/NewsletterCTA.astro';
---
<Layout title="Our Father–Daughter Story" description="A dad, a daughter, and a kitchen counter full of possibilities. Meet the family story at the heart of Two Spoons.">
  <div class="container"><header class="page-intro"><Spoons class="page-illustration" faces={true}/><span class="eyebrow">THE TWO BEHIND THE SPOONS</span><h1>A dad. A daughter.<br/><em>A delicious little dream.</em></h1><p>Before there was a name, there was a kitchen counter.<br/>And two people who really loved making something good together.</p></header></div>
  <section class="family-section"><div class="container family-grid"><div class="family-art" aria-label="Two smiling spoons represent the father and daughter who founded Two Spoons"><Spoons faces={true}/><span class="family-label dad-label">the dad</span><span class="family-label daughter-label">the daughter</span><span class="family-heart" aria-hidden="true">♡</span><span class="family-caption">two spoons. one shared table.</span></div><div class="family-copy"><span class="eyebrow">NOT JUST OUR NAME. OUR WHOLE STORY.</span><h2>We make a<br/><em>pretty good pair.</em></h2><p>Two Spoons began with a father and daughter cooking together in Haymarket, Virginia: measuring, tasting, and figuring out how to make gluten-free food that actually tastes good.</p><p>Then came the idea we couldn’t put down. What if we could turn those kitchen moments into something other families could share, too?</p><p>That’s what we’re building. Side by side, one recipe at a time.</p></div></div></section>
  <div class="container"><section class="story-body"><span class="eyebrow text-orange">DIFFERENT STRENGTHS. THE SAME TABLE.</span><h2>A family thing, <em>through and through.</em></h2><p>We both cook. We both taste. We both get a say in what comes next. The joy of Two Spoons is making something together—from a new recipe idea to the little details that make a business feel like us.</p><div class="story-two"><article class="story-person"><span class="eyebrow">ONE SPOON</span><h3>Dad brings the big picture.</h3><p>Brian brings a love of building things and keeping the wheels turning. Plans, systems, and the practical side of turning a kitchen dream into something real.</p></article><article class="story-person"><span class="eyebrow">THE OTHER SPOON</span><h3>Daughter brings the spark.</h3><p>Recipe ideas, a feel for flavor, and a sense of what’s worth another bite. The creative energy that keeps our kitchen moving forward.</p></article></div><p>Our roles overlap in the best way. This is a shared adventure—and the family at the center will always matter as much as what’s in the bag.</p></section></div>
  <section class="story-manifesto"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">WHAT WE’RE HERE TO MAKE</span><h2>Good food.<br/>More “you have to try this.”<br/><em>And a place for everyone at the table.</em></h2></div></section>
  <div class="container"><section class="story-body"><span class="eyebrow text-orange">WE’RE JUST GETTING STARTED</span><h2>You’re here for <em>the beginning.</em></h2><p>We’re still developing our first gluten-free chocolate chip cookies, banana bread, and seasoning blends. There’s plenty of tasting, learning, and recipe-tweaking ahead. We’re excited to share the journey, along with the food.</p><p>If you’ve ever cheered on a family with a big little idea, you’ll fit right in.</p><a class="text-link" href="/pantry">See what’s taking shape <Icon size={18}/></a></section></div><NewsletterCTA/>
</Layout>
